ef=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/81692-rumors-about-idigam-chronicles?p=85581#post85581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for Chris and I (and the other writers), unless we say something particularly out-there, that runs the risk of folks maybe taking it as something more than a rumor, y'know? :-P</div> </div> </div> </div> Hahaha quite the risk indeed !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T22:24:50-08:00","id":85842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/81692-rumors-about-idigam-chronicles?p=85583#post85583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that's something we can truly answer quite yet. First, stuff like that is Stew's to announce/spoil. Second, that's a hard question to answer until the actual writing of the book is firmed up a little more, and we see certain sections.<br /> <br /> One could potentially speak to it in a very broad sense, but that runs right into my first point above so I'd rather not. I'm not trying to be frustrating; I'd just rather you not feel like your post was ignored. I hate that feeling, so I try not to do it to others if at all possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood. Thanks for the response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T23:06:18-08:00","id":85853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/81692-rumors-about-idigam-chronicles?p=85577#post85577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I have learned so far from this topic , yes THIS topic !! And that's a living miracle . It's gonna have quite the changes .<br /> <br /> 1) It's gonna have the core setting on wolf-man and not on flesh-spirit<br /> 2) It's gonna get based on a core enemy with full background storyline , rather than random origin mythology .<br /> 3) Extended idigam story based chronicle , rather than werewolf-werewolf , or werewolf-spirit conflict .<br /> 4) Better quality in horror elements .</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... I'm not sure any of that is accurate.<br /> <br /> 1) There has been some (very vague) talk of updating Harmony to have a &quot;too human&quot; side as well as a &quot;too spirit&quot; side, and the possibility of the human/wolf dichotomy maybe getting more attention than it did in the W:tF core book, but the flesh/spirit dichotomy isn't going anywhere as far as I'm aware.<br /> 2) I don't quite know what this means... The Idigam (which existed in W:tF) are being framed as the main antagonists the same way the Strix were framed as the main antagonists of Blood &amp; Smoke, if that's what you mean. There has been nothing said of changing or not changing the origin myths, as far as I'm aware.<br /> 3) First of all, if you're hoping for an oWoD-style metaplot, you're out of luck. Expect more like B&amp;S - some brushed up background material, but not an ongoing plot. Second, there has been no talk of werewolf vs. werewolf conflict going anywhere as far as I'm aware. Considering the eponymous Idigam are a particularly powerful and alien kind of spirit, you can be 100% sure that werewolf vs. spirit conflict will absolutely be a big part of the brushed up background material.<br /> 4) Considering &quot;better horror&quot; is entirely subjective, this cannot be guaranteed. Also, we don't know that that's actually even a goal of the writing of Idigam Chronicle. It may be. It may not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:47:47-08:00","id":85975,"title":"","content":"Latest rumor: In keeping with the tradition of <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> having the same initials as text short-hand for an expletive (WTF), the extended title of the Idigam/Iambic/Idgit Chronicles will be <b>Savage Teeth: Forsaken Upgrade</b> or STFU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:50:49-08:00","id":85978,"title":"","content":"A lot of that is pretty close, Charlaquin (which Stew already has said, more or less, so that's not a spoiler). <br /> <br /> To expand on the last one, again as Stew said publicly, the key phrase for this book is &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt.&quot; (Or Urum Da Takus, if you prefer.) So that's something we're keeping very strongly in mind. Whether or not that constitutes &quot;better horror&quot; is up to the reader, due to that subjectivity you mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}